§§ `Article 6(2)(c): sport means sport that involves physical skill and exertion`

-- src:189 | (c) in paragraph (1)(h), “sport” means sport that involves physical skill and exertion;
-- Both sides of the condition.
#ASSERT `Art 6(2)(c) sport means sport that involves physical skill and exertion` `G2 facts: a sport that involves physical skill and exertion`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(2)(c) sport means sport that involves physical skill and exertion` `G2 facts: a pastime that involves no physical skill and exertion`
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the advancement of public participation in sport`) `G2 facts: a sport that involves physical skill and exertion`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the advancement of public participation in sport`) `G2 facts: a pastime that involves no physical skill and exertion`
-- The recorded head (h) with the exertion not stated: the clause cannot be applied, so the encoding refuses.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the advancement of public participation in sport`) `G2 facts: nothing relevant` BECAUSE "Article 6(2)(c) was not given whether the sport involves physical skill and exertion"
-- The condition belongs to head (h) only: a purpose recorded under education is unaffected by it.
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the advancement of education`) `G2 facts: a pastime that involves no physical skill and exertion`
-- A purpose recorded under (h) that is not sport may still be within another paragraph by a clarification (here 6(2)(a), the relief of suffering).
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the advancement of public participation in sport`) `G2 facts: the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering`

§§ `Article 6(2)(d): paragraph (1)(i) applies only to facilities for people in need or open to the public at large`

-- src:190 | (d) paragraph (1)(i) applies only in relation to recreational facilities or activities that are –
-- src:191 | (i) primarily intended for persons who have need of them by reason of their age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage, or
