#ASSERT `Art 6(2)(d) paragraph (1)(i) applies` `G2 facts: facilities primarily for people in need`
#ASSERT `Art 6(2)(d) paragraph (1)(i) applies` `G2 facts: facilities open to the public at large`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(2)(d) paragraph (1)(i) applies` `G2 facts: facilities neither for people in need nor open to the public at large`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 6(2)(d) paragraph (1)(i) applies` `G2 facts: facilities not for people in need, openness not stated` BECAUSE "Article 6(2)(d) was not given whether the facilities or activities are primarily for people in need or open to the public at large"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 6(2)(d) paragraph (1)(i) applies` `G2 facts: nothing relevant` BECAUSE "Article 6(2)(d) was not given whether the facilities or activities are primarily for people in need or open to the public at large"

§§ `Article 6(1)(i): the object of improving the conditions of life, and 6(2)(d), each on both sides`

-- src:176 | (i) the provision of recreational facilities, or the organisation of recreational activities, with the object of improving the conditions of life for the persons for whom the facilities or activities are primarily intended;
-- The head needs BOTH: the object, and one of the two conditions of 6(2)(d).  Object stated and 6(2)(d)(i) or (ii) stated to hold: admitted.
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities`) `G2 facts: facilities for people in need, with the object of improving the conditions of life`
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities`) `G2 facts: facilities open to the public at large, with the object of improving the conditions of life`
-- Object stated NOT to hold: not admitted, whichever of 6(2)(d)'s conditions holds (the amusement arcade open to all and not for improving conditions of life), and whether or not they are stated.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities`) `G2 facts: facilities for people in need, without the object of improving the conditions of life`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities`) `G2 facts: facilities open to the public at large, without the object of improving the conditions of life`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities`) `G2 facts: without the object of improving the conditions of life, openness and need not stated`
-- Object stated to hold but neither 6(2)(d) condition: not admitted.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities`) `G2 facts: the object of improving the conditions of life, facilities neither for people in need nor open to the public at large`
-- Object stated, 6(2)(d) not stated: the 6(2)(d) refusal stands.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities`) `G2 facts: the object of improving the conditions of life, openness and need not stated` BECAUSE "Article 6(2)(d) was not given whether the facilities or activities are primarily for people in need or open to the public at large"
-- Object not stated: a 6(2)(d) condition that holds cannot decide the head, so the encoding refuses; 6(2)(d) stated not to hold on both alternatives decides it as not admitted.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities`) `G2 facts: facilities primarily for people in need` BECAUSE "Article 6(1)(i) was not given whether the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities`) `G2 facts: facilities open to the public at large` BECAUSE "Article 6(1)(i) was not given whether the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities`) `G2 facts: nothing relevant` BECAUSE "Article 6(1)(i) was not given whether the facilities or activities have the object of improving the conditions of life"
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the provision of recreational facilities or the organisation of recreational activities`) `G2 facts: facilities neither for people in need nor open to the public at large`
-- The function that carries both conditions, called directly.
#ASSERT `Art 6(1)(i) paragraph (1)(i) is met` `G2 facts: facilities for people in need, with the object of improving the conditions of life`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1)(i) paragraph (1)(i) is met` `G2 facts: facilities open to the public at large, without the object of improving the conditions of life`

§§ `Article 6(2)(e): paragraph (1)(n) includes relief given by the provision of accommodation or care (FORK F2.14)`

-- src:181 | (n) the relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage;
-- src:193 | (e) paragraph (1)(n) includes relief given by the provision of accommodation or care;
-- Label: default ruled by the owner (Meng), 2026-10-27.  Reading A (taken, declaratory): relief given by accommodation or care is within (n) only as relief of those in need.  Reading B (widening): the
-- provision of accommodation or care is within (n) without more.  Four fact-sets: the witness (accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need), relief of those in need given by accommodation or care,
-- the same recorded by a caller that predates the separate fact (the seventh column only), and nothing relevant.
-- Reading A, the clause itself.
#ASSERT `Art 6(2)(e) paragraph (1)(n) includes the purpose, as relief given by accommodation or care` `G2 facts: relief by the provision of accommodation or care` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 6(2)(e) paragraph (1)(n) includes the purpose, as relief given by accommodation or care` `G2 facts: relief of those in need given by accommodation or care, the provision not separately recorded` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(2)(e) paragraph (1)(n) includes the purpose, as relief given by accommodation or care` `G2 facts: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(2)(e) paragraph (1)(n) includes the purpose, as relief given by accommodation or care` `G2 facts: nothing relevant` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
-- Reading B, the clause itself.
#ASSERT `Art 6(2)(e) paragraph (1)(n) includes the purpose, as relief given by accommodation or care` `G2 facts: relief by the provision of accommodation or care` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.14 read as B`
#ASSERT `Art 6(2)(e) paragraph (1)(n) includes the purpose, as relief given by accommodation or care` `G2 facts: relief of those in need given by accommodation or care, the provision not separately recorded` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.14 read as B`
#ASSERT `Art 6(2)(e) paragraph (1)(n) includes the purpose, as relief given by accommodation or care` `G2 facts: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.14 read as B`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(2)(e) paragraph (1)(n) includes the purpose, as relief given by accommodation or care` `G2 facts: nothing relevant` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.14 read as B`
-- Each reading's private rule, called directly.
#ASSERT `reading A of Article 6(2)(e): only as relief of those in need` `G2 facts: relief by the provision of accommodation or care`
#ASSERT `reading A of Article 6(2)(e): only as relief of those in need` `G2 facts: relief of those in need given by accommodation or care, the provision not separately recorded`
#ASSERT NOT `reading A of Article 6(2)(e): only as relief of those in need` `G2 facts: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need`
#ASSERT NOT `reading A of Article 6(2)(e): only as relief of those in need` `G2 facts: nothing relevant`
#ASSERT `reading B of Article 6(2)(e): the provision of accommodation or care suffices` `G2 facts: relief by the provision of accommodation or care`
#ASSERT `reading B of Article 6(2)(e): the provision of accommodation or care suffices` `G2 facts: relief of those in need given by accommodation or care, the provision not separately recorded`
#ASSERT `reading B of Article 6(2)(e): the provision of accommodation or care suffices` `G2 facts: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need`
#ASSERT NOT `reading B of Article 6(2)(e): the provision of accommodation or care suffices` `G2 facts: nothing relevant`
-- Reading B is reading A OR the new fact, so the two readings differ only where the eleventh field is TRUE and the seventh is FALSE.  Stated on each of the four fact-sets.
#ASSERT (`reading B of Article 6(2)(e): the provision of accommodation or care suffices` `G2 facts: relief by the provision of accommodation or care`) EQUALS ((`reading A of Article 6(2)(e): only as relief of those in need` `G2 facts: relief by the provision of accommodation or care`) OR (`G2 facts: relief by the provision of accommodation or care`)'s `the purpose is the provision of accommodation or care`)
#ASSERT (`reading B of Article 6(2)(e): the provision of accommodation or care suffices` `G2 facts: relief of those in need given by accommodation or care, the provision not separately recorded`) EQUALS ((`reading A of Article 6(2)(e): only as relief of those in need` `G2 facts: relief of those in need given by accommodation or care, the provision not separately recorded`) OR (`G2 facts: relief of those in need given by accommodation or care, the provision not separately recorded`)'s `the purpose is the provision of accommodation or care`)
#ASSERT (`reading B of Article 6(2)(e): the provision of accommodation or care suffices` `G2 facts: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need`) EQUALS ((`reading A of Article 6(2)(e): only as relief of those in need` `G2 facts: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need`) OR (`G2 facts: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need`)'s `the purpose is the provision of accommodation or care`)
#ASSERT (`reading B of Article 6(2)(e): the provision of accommodation or care suffices` `G2 facts: nothing relevant`) EQUALS ((`reading A of Article 6(2)(e): only as relief of those in need` `G2 facts: nothing relevant`) OR (`G2 facts: nothing relevant`)'s `the purpose is the provision of accommodation or care`)
-- Through the clarifications of 6(2) as a whole.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(2) a clarification brings the purpose within a head` `G2 facts: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
#ASSERT `Art 6(2) a clarification brings the purpose within a head` `G2 facts: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.14 read as B`
-- The witness is a purpose recorded under no head: it is a charitable purpose on B and not on A.  The other three fact-sets give the same answer on both readings.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `a G2 purpose that falls under no head` `G2 facts: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need`
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.14 read as B` `a G2 purpose that falls under no head` `G2 facts: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need`
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `a G2 purpose that falls under no head` `G2 facts: relief by the provision of accommodation or care`
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.14 read as B` `a G2 purpose that falls under no head` `G2 facts: relief by the provision of accommodation or care`
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `a G2 purpose that falls under no head` `G2 facts: relief of those in need given by accommodation or care, the provision not separately recorded`
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.14 read as B` `a G2 purpose that falls under no head` `G2 facts: relief of those in need given by accommodation or care, the provision not separately recorded`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `a G2 purpose that falls under no head` `G2 facts: nothing relevant`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.14 read as B` `a G2 purpose that falls under no head` `G2 facts: nothing relevant`
-- A purpose the caller records under head (n) is within it on both readings, whatever the facts say about accommodation or care: the head is the caller's determination that it relieves those in need.
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage`) `G2 facts: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need`
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.14 read as B` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the relief of those in need by reason of age, ill-health, disability, financial hardship or other disadvantage`) `G2 facts: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need`
-- Article 6(5) excludes a political purpose "irrespective of whether it would otherwise fall within paragraph (1)": the widening does not reach it.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.14 read as B` `a G2 political purpose` `G2 facts: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need`

§§ `Article 6(2)(f): the advancement of any philosophical belief is analogous to the purpose in paragraph (1)(c), for the purposes of paragraph (1)(p)`

-- src:194 | (f) for the purposes of paragraph (1)(p), the advancement of any philosophical belief (whether or not involving belief in a god) is analogous to the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(c).
-- Such a purpose is within (p) on either reading of F2.5: it is a charitable purpose.
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `a G2 purpose of advancing a philosophical belief` `G2 facts: nothing relevant`
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.5 read as B` `a G2 purpose of advancing a philosophical belief` `G2 facts: nothing relevant`
-- The discriminating case of F2.5, IP11: a humanist association's purpose is within (c) only on the second reading.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6 the purpose is within the advancement of religion` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `a G2 purpose of advancing a philosophical belief`
#ASSERT `Art 6 the purpose is within the advancement of religion` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.5 read as B` `a G2 purpose of advancing a philosophical belief`
-- A purpose recorded under (c) itself is within (c) on both readings.
#ASSERT `Art 6 the purpose is within the advancement of religion` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the advancement of religion`)
#ASSERT `Art 6 the purpose is within the advancement of religion` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.5 read as B` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the advancement of religion`)
-- A purpose recorded under another head is not within (c) on either reading, even if the philosophical flag is off.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6 the purpose is within the advancement of religion` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the advancement of education`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6 the purpose is within the advancement of religion` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.5 read as B` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the advancement of education`)
-- The entity form (IP11), over a list of purposes.
#ASSERT `Art 6 the entity has a purpose within the advancement of religion` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 entity with these purposes` (LIST (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the advancement of education`), (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the advancement of religion`)))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6 the entity has a purpose within the advancement of religion` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 entity with these purposes` (LIST (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the advancement of education`), `a G2 purpose of advancing a philosophical belief`))
#ASSERT `Art 6 the entity has a purpose within the advancement of religion` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.5 read as B` (`a G2 entity with these purposes` (LIST (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the advancement of education`), `a G2 purpose of advancing a philosophical belief`))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6 the entity has a purpose within the advancement of religion` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 entity with these purposes` EMPTY)

§§ `Article 6(1)(l): equality and diversity`

-- src:179 | (l) the promotion of equality and diversity;
-- First reading: both must be promoted.
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the promotion of equality and diversity`) `G2 facts: equality and diversity both promoted`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the promotion of equality and diversity`) `G2 facts: diversity promoted, equality not`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the promotion of equality and diversity`) `G2 facts: equality not promoted, diversity not stated`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the promotion of equality and diversity`) `G2 facts: equality promoted, diversity not stated` BECAUSE "Article 6(1)(l) was not given whether the purpose promotes equality and diversity"
-- Second reading: either suffices.
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.11 read as B` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the promotion of equality and diversity`) `G2 facts: diversity promoted, equality not`
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.11 read as B` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the promotion of equality and diversity`) `G2 facts: equality promoted, diversity not stated`
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.11 read as B` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the promotion of equality and diversity`) `G2 facts: equality not stated, diversity promoted`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.11 read as B` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the promotion of equality and diversity`) `G2 facts: equality not promoted, diversity not stated` BECAUSE "Article 6(1)(l) was not given whether the purpose promotes equality and diversity"
-- Head (l) recorded and neither idea stated: the clause cannot be applied on either reading, so the encoding refuses.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the promotion of equality and diversity`) `G2 facts: nothing relevant` BECAUSE "Article 6(1)(l) was not given whether the purpose promotes equality and diversity"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.11 read as B` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the promotion of equality and diversity`) `G2 facts: nothing relevant` BECAUSE "Article 6(1)(l) was not given whether the purpose promotes equality and diversity"

§§ `Article 6(5): political purposes`

-- src:201 | (5) The purpose of advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election to any office, whether in Jersey or elsewhere, is neither a charitable purpose nor a purpose ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose, irrespective of whether it would otherwise fall within paragraph (1) or Article 5(1)(a)(ii).
#ASSERT `Art 6(5) the purpose is neither charitable nor ancillary` `a G2 political purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(5) the purpose is neither charitable nor ancillary` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the advancement of education`)
-- Neither charitable "irrespective of whether it would otherwise fall within paragraph (1)": a political purpose recorded under education is not a charitable purpose.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 political purpose recorded under` `the advancement of education`) `G2 facts: nothing relevant`
-- Nor is a political purpose that a clarification of 6(2) would otherwise bring within a head.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `a G2 political purpose` `G2 facts: the prevention or relief of sickness, disease or human suffering`
-- Nor is it within (c) even when recorded there.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6 the purpose is within the advancement of religion` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`a G2 political purpose recorded under` `the advancement of religion`)
-- Pairs.
#ASSERT `Art 6(1) the purpose with its facts is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`the G2 pair of a purpose with nothing relevant recorded under` `the advancement of education`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(1) the purpose with its facts is a charitable purpose` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` (`the G2 purpose` `a G2 political purpose` `with` `G2 facts: nothing relevant`)

§§ `Article 6(3) and (4): the States' power and its limit`

GIVEN adds1 IS A BOOLEAN
      adds2 IS A BOOLEAN
      explanatory IS A BOOLEAN
      amends IS A BOOLEAN
      alters IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Content of Regulations under Article 6(3)`
`Regulations that` adds1 `, add to (2)` adds2 `, explain` explanatory `, amend` amends `, alter (5)` alters MEANS
    `Content of Regulations under Article 6(3)` OF adds1, adds2, explanatory, amends, alters

-- src:198 | (4) The power under paragraph (3) does not include power –
-- src:199 | (a) to amend or restrict the effect of any of paragraphs (1)(a) to (p) and (2)(a) to (f); or
-- src:200 | (b) to alter the effect of paragraph (5).
-- Within the power: add a sub-paragraph to (1).
#ASSERT `Art 6(4) the Regulations are within the power of Article 6(3)` (`Regulations that` TRUE `, add to (2)` FALSE `, explain` FALSE `, amend` FALSE `, alter (5)` FALSE)
-- Within the power: add explanatory sub-paragraphs to (2) for sub-paragraphs added to (1) (earlier or in the same Regulations).
#ASSERT `Art 6(4) the Regulations are within the power of Article 6(3)` (`Regulations that` FALSE `, add to (2)` TRUE `, explain` TRUE `, amend` FALSE `, alter (5)` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 6(4) the Regulations are within the power of Article 6(3)` (`Regulations that` TRUE `, add to (2)` TRUE `, explain` TRUE `, amend` FALSE `, alter (5)` FALSE)
-- Outside the power: a sub-paragraph added to (2) that is not explanatory of a sub-paragraph added to (1).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(4) the Regulations are within the power of Article 6(3)` (`Regulations that` FALSE `, add to (2)` TRUE `, explain` FALSE `, amend` FALSE `, alter (5)` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(4) the Regulations are within the power of Article 6(3)` (`Regulations that` TRUE `, add to (2)` TRUE `, explain` FALSE `, amend` FALSE `, alter (5)` FALSE)
-- Outside the power: 6(4)(a) amend or restrict the effect of (1)(a) to (p) or (2)(a) to (f).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(4) the Regulations are within the power of Article 6(3)` (`Regulations that` TRUE `, add to (2)` FALSE `, explain` FALSE `, amend` TRUE `, alter (5)` FALSE)
-- Outside the power: 6(4)(b) alter the effect of paragraph (5).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(4) the Regulations are within the power of Article 6(3)` (`Regulations that` TRUE `, add to (2)` FALSE `, explain` FALSE `, amend` FALSE `, alter (5)` TRUE)
-- Nothing added is no exercise of the power.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(4) the Regulations are within the power of Article 6(3)` (`Regulations that` FALSE `, add to (2)` FALSE `, explain` FALSE `, amend` FALSE `, alter (5)` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(4) the Regulations are within the power of Article 6(3)` (`Regulations that` FALSE `, add to (2)` FALSE `, explain` TRUE `, amend` FALSE `, alter (5)` FALSE)

-- src:195 | (3) The States may, on the recommendation of the Commissioner, by Regulations –
-- src:196 | (a) add sub-paragraphs to paragraph (1);
-- src:197 | (b) add sub-paragraphs to paragraph (2) making explanatory provision in relation to any sub-paragraphs so added to paragraph (1).
-- The States may make valid Regulations only on the Commissioner's recommendation and within the limit.
#ASSERT `Art 6(3) the States may make the Regulations` TRUE (`Regulations that` TRUE `, add to (2)` FALSE `, explain` FALSE `, amend` FALSE `, alter (5)` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(3) the States may make the Regulations` FALSE (`Regulations that` TRUE `, add to (2)` FALSE `, explain` FALSE `, amend` FALSE `, alter (5)` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 6(3) the States may make the Regulations` TRUE (`Regulations that` TRUE `, add to (2)` FALSE `, explain` FALSE `, amend` TRUE `, alter (5)` FALSE)

-- On the Commissioner's recommendation the States may make the Regulations: the permission stands until used, and using it is fulfilment.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 6(3) the States may add a sub-paragraph to Article 6(1) or (2)` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the States` DOES (`make Regulations adding sub-paragraphs to the list of charitable purposes or to its explanations` `the States`) AT 9

-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `Art 6(3) the States may add a sub-paragraph to Article 6(1) or (2)` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 1000)

-- Without the recommendation there is no power, and so nothing owed or permitted.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
